# 15. Production Secure NAT Setup (BEST PRACTICE)

```bash id="prod1"
sudo nft add table ip nat

sudo nft add chain ip nat prerouting '{ type nat hook prerouting priority -100 ; }'

sudo nft add chain ip nat postrouting '{ type nat hook postrouting priority 100 ; }'

sudo nft add rule ip nat prerouting iif "eth0" tcp dport 80 dnat to 192.168.1.10:80

sudo nft add rule ip nat postrouting oif "eth0" masquerade
```

---

# 16. Security Summary

| Feature              | Secure | Unsecure |
| -------------------- | ------ | -------- |
| Port-specific DNAT   | ✅      | ❌        |
| Interface-based SNAT | ✅      | ❌        |
| Masquerade use       | ✅      | ⚠        |
| Full NAT exposure    | ❌      | ❌❌       |
| State tracking       | ✅      | ❌        |

---

# 17. Best Practices

✔ Always use specific ports in DNAT
✔ Use masquerade for dynamic IP
✔ Always configure FORWARD chain
✔ Never expose full subnet
✔ Use state tracking
✔ Log NAT traffic for debugging
✔ Test from external network

